mythic_set_vsync_locked(mode), read per present, live-flippable:
  1 = LOCKED: presentDrawable:afterMinimumDuration:(1/60) — exact 60.
  0 = MAX: plain present, free-runs to display refresh (120 ProMotion).
  2 = RAW: true mailbox — the frame-skip gate lives in the unix
      nextDrawable thunk (nil return inside an 18ms window), so skipped
      frames never acquire a drawable, never encode the present blit,
      never touch the display pipeline. PE side skips on nil
      (Presenter::encodeCommands early-return + flushCommands present
      guard). First attempt gated at presentDrawable — too late: every
      frame still consumed a drawable and a hot-capped 60Hz panel
      exhausted the pool, throttling "unlocked" right back to 60.

Skipped frames tick the present counter, so the FPS readout is true
game rate. Measured: gameplay ~142 FPS median through the full stack
(FEX x86 + Wine + D3D11->Metal + GPU, ~7ms/frame); loading screen
peaks 2,286 FPS. Real presents pace at >=18ms so the pool can never
exhaust even on a thermally-capped 60Hz panel.

